.TH "SOPLOS-STORE" "1" "2026-11-16" "Soplos Linux" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
soplos-store \- Modern software center for Soplos Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B soplos-store
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIFILE\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B soplos-store
is the primary software center application for Soplos Linux installations.
It provides a unified, beautiful, and secure interface for discovering, installing,
updating, and removing applications across multiple packaging formats:
.IP \[bu] 2
Native Debian packages (APT).
.IP \[bu]
Flatpak applications from Flathub.
.IP \[bu]
Snap packages from the Snap Store.
.IP \[bu]
Standalone AppImages integrated into ~/AppImages with desktop launchers.
.IP \[bu]
System firmware updates via fwupd and LVFS.
.IP \[bu]
Drivers, a section of the sidebar that is turned on in Settings: the graphics cards of the machine and the NVIDIA driver branches (installed from the Debian repositories or NVIDIA's own CUDA repository, with the patches kernels 7.x need), plus the Mesa and firmware packages of AMD and Intel cards, and pages for printers, scanners, graphics tablets, 2-in-1 laptops (the tablet-soplos package of each Soplos edition), laptops (with a section for Apple Mac computers) and other hardware, each with the official page of its makers.
.P
In Settings the user chooses which sources the Store shows (Flatpak, Snap and AppImage: with one turned off the Store shows nothing of it and does not look for its updates), whether the Drivers section is shown, the theme (Automatic follows the one of the desktop) and which of Featured, Popular and Trending appear on the home page. The Updates page lists the packages that apt would upgrade, as PackageKit and GNOME Software see them, and tells which packages go out and which come in with them.
.P
Designed to be lightweight and responsive with Tauri 2, Rust, and modern web technologies,
offering desktop-agnostic integration across XFCE 4.20, KDE Plasma 6, and GNOME 48+.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-updates
Launch the application directly into the Updates view.
.TP
.B \-\-tray
Run in background mode as an update notifier with a system tray icon and desktop notifications.
.TP
.B \-\-check-updates
Execute an automated background check for available updates and update the cache (invoked by systemd user timer).
.TP
.B \-\-privileged-refresh
Internal Polkit-authenticated task for passwordless repository synchronization.
.TP
.B \-\-privileged \fIACTION\fR [\fIARGS...\fR]
Internal Polkit-authenticated task for package management actions (install, remove, update).
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show summary of options.
.SH SUPPORTED FILES
When launched with a file path as an argument,
.B soplos-store
inspects and offers one-click installation for:
.IP \[bu] 2
.B .deb
Debian binary package files.
.IP \[bu]
.B .flatpak
Flatpak single-file bundle archives.
.IP \[bu]
.B .flatpakref
Flatpak repository application references.
.IP \[bu]
.B .snap
Snap package files.
.IP \[bu]
.B .AppImage
Linux standalone AppImage executables (automatically integrated into ~/AppImages).
.SH KEYBOARD SHORTCUTS
.TP
.B F1
About dialog.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Q
Quit the application.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Tab, Ctrl+Shift+Tab
Next or previous section.
.TP
.B F5, Ctrl+R
Reload.
.TP
.B Ctrl+F
Search.
.TP
.B Escape, Alt+Left
Back.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/xdg/autostart/soplos-store-tray.desktop
System autostart entry for the update notifier tray service.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/user/soplos-store-updates.timer
Systemd user timer triggering periodic background update checks.
.TP
.I /usr/share/polkit-1/actions/org.soplos.store.policy
Polkit policy defining administrator privileges for APT operations.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/soplos-store/
User-specific cache directory for catalog data and update status.
